# Line-ending policy.
#
# LF everywhere, on every platform, including Windows checkouts.  Two reasons:
#
# 1. core.autocrlf=true is the default on Windows, which would otherwise rewrite
#    LF to CRLF in the working tree.  Then a patch that applies cleanly in CI
#    shows as a whole-file diff locally, and a test that asserts on line endings
#    passes here and fails there.
# 2. Nothing in this package is a shell script, but a contributor adding one --
#    a dev helper, a CI entry point -- must not have to discover that a CRLF
#    shebang breaks bash.  Forcing it globally means they cannot get it wrong.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content; the explicit binary entries below
# are belt and braces for the file types this package will accumulate if people
# start committing weights.

*               text=auto eol=lf

*.py            text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.toml          text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.cfg           text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.jsonl         text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf

# Never line-ending-translate these.  Model weights and tokenizer vocabularies
# are gitignored today; if someone force-adds one, translating it corrupts it.
*.safetensors   binary
*.pt            binary
*.pth           binary
*.bin           binary
*.npz           binary
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.zip           binary
*.gz            binary
